diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..39a13aa 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,39 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP browser tools
+
+The shared layout registers browser tools when `document.modelContext.registerTool`
+exists. Unsupported browsers retain the regular controls. The implementation uses
+[the WebMCP imperative API](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/) and
+[experimental declarative form attributes](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api).
+No MCP server or browser extension is bundled.
+
+| Tool | Inputs | Availability |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `query` | All pages using the shared layout; opens search results |
+| `get_reading_list` | None | Shared layout; opens the current session list |
+| `set_article_saved` | `slug`, `saved` | Shared layout; explicitly saves or removes an article |
+| `get_coffee_brew` | None | Coffee Alchemy article |
+| `get_plant_stats` | None | Silent Architects article |
+| `get_tide_levels` | None | Coastal Pulse article |
+| `get_article_popularity` | None | Super Bowl LX article; supplies the article ID |
+
+Open flyouts also expose `search_articles_form`, `get_reading_list_form`, and
+per-article removal forms. The article bookmark form exposes an explicit
+save/remove action. These forms use `toolname`, `tooldescription`,
+`toolparamdescription`, and `toolautosubmit`; agent submissions receive structured
+results through the native submit event's `respondWith()` method. Human submissions
+use the same operations and show failures in the UI.
+
+All requests respect Astro's configured base path and use the existing session.
+Reading-list writes accept `add`, `remove`, or the legacy `toggle` action; explicit
+add/remove operations are idempotent. Bookmarks and open lists synchronize after
+writes. Imperative registrations and in-flight executions are aborted during Astro
+page transitions; article utilities are available only on their relevant article.
+
+The diagnostic article endpoints intentionally simulate failures. Coffee may return
+500, plants may return 431 when the article's oversized cookies are present, and
+tides redirects to an absent endpoint. Tools report HTTP status, final URL,
+redirect information, and any JSON response rather than reporting false success.
